# =========================================================
# RANK 2 - "Stuck"
# GATE: char son_1, rank 2, period evening, room son_room_1
# =========================================================

~ start

$> locals.tone = 0
$> GameState.location("Miles' room · Evening")
$> GameState.sprite("son_1", "desk")

The same screen he was on an hour ago. Same boss.

Mom: [#mood=neutral, #pose=standing] Still at it.

Miles: [#mood=strain, #pose=desk] It's got a second phase.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] A second phase.

Miles: [#mood=strain] Everyone says it's easy. It's not easy, they're just — the dodge window is one frame.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] One frame.

Miles: [#mood=strain] You can't see it. It's a timing thing. It's muscle memory.

He dies. Same place. He doesn't react.

Miles: [#mood=averted] I know. I know.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] I didn't say anything.

Miles: [#mood=averted] You were going to.

She comes further in. The bed's right there.

Miles: [#mood=strain] It's the third one. The meteor one. You have to be already moving.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] Show me the meteor one.

- Sit on the floor by the chair.
	$> locals.tone += 1
	She lowers herself down, back against the desk leg, close enough that her shoulder is at his elbow.
	Miles: [#mood=surprised] Oh — okay.
	Miles: [#mood=strain] It's — you won't see it from down there.
	Mom: [#mood=neutral] Then tell me when it's coming.
	Miles: [#mood=flushed] ...Right. Okay.
- Sit on the edge of the bed.
	She sits on the mattress, facing the screen.
	Miles: [#mood=strain] It's fine. You can sit.
	She can see the screen from there. Barely.
- Stay in the doorway.
	Mom: [#mood=neutral] Go on. I've got time.
	He turns back. He's not going to start while she's watching.

He restarts. His shoulders are up around his ears.

Miles: [#mood=strain] Meteor. Meteor — now.

She watches him dodge badly. The bar empties.

Miles: [#mood=strain] That was the one. That was it.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] You were early.

Miles: [#mood=surprised] How do you know that.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] You flinched before it moved.

He stares at her. Then turns back and restarts without a word.

The second time he waits. He gets through.

Miles: [#mood=surprised] Oh my god.

Mom: [#mood=soft] There.

He doesn't say anything. He's still playing. His knee is against her shoulder now and neither of them moves it.

$> GameState.apply("miles_r2", locals.tone)

$> GameState.rank_card("son_1", 2)

=> END

